Okay, so Giuseppe has a big plywood sheet that's 22 units by 15 units. He wants to cut out as many smaller rectangular blanks as possible, each of size 3x5. The question is asking how to do this optimally. Hmm, let's think through this step by step.

First, I need to figure out how many 3x5 rectangles can fit into a 22x15 sheet. But since the sheet is larger than the smaller rectangles, there's going to be some arrangement that allows for the maximum number. But I need to make sure I don't just do a simple division because maybe depending on how you arrange them, you can fit more.

